{#
   THE SUB-VENUE CONTROL — one control, every screen that carries a sub-venue.

   ⚠️ **It filters what is shown. It is never an authorization control.** The help
   line says so on screen because the question gets asked; `VenueContext` resolves
   a *display* scope and the voters decide access separately.

   Parameters:
     venue_context      the array from `VenueContext::forRequest()` or `::single()`
     list_route         route this control submits to
     list_route_params  route parameters, if it needs any
     list_query         current query string, re-emitted as hidden inputs so the
                        sub-venue does not silently drop search, facets or page
     allow_all          include "all sub-venues" (default true). ⚠️ Screens that
                        **edit** venue-scoped rows must pass false: opening hours
                        are stored per venue, so "all" names no row to write, and
                        offering it is a control that cannot succeed.

   ⚠️ Changed in S131: the inline `onchange="this.form.submit()"` became
   `autosubmit_controller`, and the four hardcoded French strings became keys —
   a filter's every label, option and help line goes through the five catalogues.
#}
<form class="venue-context" method="get" action="{{ path(list_route, list_route_params|default({})) }}">
    {% for key, value in list_query|default({}) %}{% if key != 'location' %}<input type="hidden" name="{{ key }}" value="{{ value }}">{% endif %}{% endfor %}
    <label for="venue-context-select">{{ 'venue_context.label'|trans }}</label>
    <select id="venue-context-select"
            name="location"
            data-controller="autosubmit"
            data-action="change->autosubmit#submit">
        {% if allow_all|default(true) %}
            <option value="all"{{ venue_context.location == 'all' ? ' selected' : '' }}>{{ 'venue_context.all'|trans }}</option>
        {% endif %}
        {% for venue in venue_context.venues %}
            <option value="{{ venue.slug }}"{{ venue_context.location == venue.slug ? ' selected' : '' }}>{{ venue.name }}</option>
        {% endfor %}
    </select>
    <noscript><button class="ml-btn" type="submit">{{ 'venue_context.apply'|trans }}</button></noscript>
    <p>{{ 'venue_context.not_a_right'|trans }}</p>
</form>
